---
title: Prefabs
---
A piece of map designed by hand, dropped into a generated one [[t:198-200 s:22]].

## The rule
```text
in a room:     pick random rooms until one is big enough; stamp it at the room's center
on open floor: pick random spots until the whole prefab lies on floor; stamp it there
down the middle: stamp it over the center columns of the map
```

With rooms, the talk’s way is to go through the room list for a room bigger than the prefab [[t:203-205]]. On a map without rooms it picks random locations and looks whether the prefab will fit [[t:205-207]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5

## Controls
@@control shape
`vault` is the talk’s treasure ringed by traps [[c14:149-155 t:200-201]]. `spine` is our stand-in for the fortifications the talk’s combined map gets: a hall of our own design [[own]].
@@control place
`room` puts it at the center of a random room that is big enough [[c14:105-109]], `open-area` wherever a random spot has floor under all of it [[c15:42-50]], and `center` down the middle of the map, as the combined map’s is [[c09:122-124]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

Treasure and traps count as walkable, so a vault changes none of the traits its map had [[own]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

Both of the talk’s placement loops end only when the prefab has been placed [[c14:106-124 c15:41-67]]. On a map with no room big enough, or no clear patch of floor the right size, they never end; ours stops and records the seed [[own]].

